notes: 'This exact source preparation uses8.4gNaHCO3 with100mLwater,CO2saturation
  andsealedautoclaving. The original amount iswateradded,notanexplicitmake-uptofinal100mL.
  Generic84g/Lstock owner and its J451autoclavedunderCO2context do not establish identical
  finalvolume or priorCO2saturation. A distinct source-defined operational identity
  preserves these facts rather than silentlymergingbyrounded1Mmolarity. Source occurrence
  IDs and receiving doses remain in the campaign ledger/CultureMech; no complete medium
  is asserted as thisstock. New0/0statsmeanmembershipnotyetrefreshed,notobservedabsence.
  Cross-lane deduplication: NBRC1257 and NBRC1321 both specify 8.4 g NaHCO3 plus 100
  mL distilled water, CO2 saturation and autoclaving in tightly sealed CO2-filled
  bottles. The source qualification and complete preparation establish the same stock;
  neither source states make-up to a final 100 mL. ''Bicarbonate solution (1.0 M)***'':
  NBRC1321 uses this exact string as the receiving-table pointer to its *** footnote.
  The text gives a nominal strength but does not name the sodium salt, added-water
  recipe, or CO2 saturation that defines this proposed preparation. The *** footnote
  supplies NaHCO3 8.4 g plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation, and autoclaving
  in tightly sealed CO2-filled bottles. It is a valid source pointer and broader material
  description, but is not an identity-bearing standalone name for this particular
  CO2-conditioned stock. Retain the original sourced REJECTED_LABEL entry and resolve
  only the explicitly bound source occurrence, rather than claim exact identity for
  that token outside its footnote.MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 / CHEM-COMP-006 (#1237),
  individual label assessments:  ''Bicarbonate solution***'': NBRC1257 uses this exact
  string as its receiving-table *** pointer, without even the nominal strength. Its
  *** footnote positively specifies the same NaHCO3 8.4 g plus 100 mL distilled water
  and CO2 saturation/sealed autoclaving as NBRC1321. The bare token does not identify
  that sodium/quantity/CO2 preparation independently of the footnote. Retain its exact
  sourced REJECTED_LABEL entry as a non-name for this specific owner, while retaining
  the positive source-occurrence assignment and source-supported NBRC1257/NBRC1321
  union. No competing preferred owner of either exact token was found in the explicitly
  checked current mapped directory and worker01 proposal set, so no owned-name suppression
  is proposed. These dispositions concern name applicability to this specific preparation,
  not rejection of bicarbonate as a material. The reported 1.0 M remains nominal:
  100 mL is added water, not verified final solution volume; dissolved CO2 amount/speciation
  is unquantified. Carbon dioxide remains a source-listed material input because the
  solution is explicitly saturated, independently of the CO2 headspace condition.'
